course: dictionary
lesson: 11819
title: Binoculars and binocular
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can work in more than one way. Binoculars is a noun, the name of a tool. Binocular is an adjective, a describing word, and it means using both eyes. The words around it show you which one you have.
explain: «Mia used a pair of binoculars to watch the owl in the tree.» Here binoculars is the thing she held. Notice «a pair of»: binoculars come as one tool with two small telescopes, one for each eye, so we say them as a pair.
explain: «The binocular view from the hill let Sam see the whole valley.» Here binocular describes the view, so it means seen with both eyes. To check, put your meaning into the sentence: «seen with both eyes view» sounds odd, but the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Binoculars are a tool with two small telescopes joined together, one for each eye.
fact: Binoculars make far-away things look bigger and closer.
fact: «Binoculars» is plural, so we say «a pair of binoculars».
fact: «Binocular» is an adjective meaning using both eyes.
fact: Never look at the Sun through binoculars, because it can blind you.
exercise: «Dad bought a pair of binoculars for our trip to the coast.» What are binoculars? | A pair of gloves for cold hands | A kind of bird that lives by the sea | A map of the coast | *A tool with two small telescopes, one for each eye
exercise: «Lily used her binoculars to watch the ships far out at sea.» What do binoculars do? | *They make far-away things look bigger and closer | They keep the rain off your face | They make near things look smaller | They make the sea sound louder
exercise: «The binocular view let Tom see both sides of the lake clearly.» What does binocular mean in this sentence? | *Using both eyes | Very dark | Using one eye only | Made of wood
test: «Never look at the Sun through binoculars, because it can blind you.» Why must you never do this? | It makes the Sun too cold | It makes the Sun look smaller | It turns the sky green | *It can blind you
test: In «Her binocular vision helped her catch the ball», which word is the adjective? | *binocular | ball | vision | catch
exam: «The birdwatchers agreed: a pair of binoculars is the best gift for a nature lover.» Why do we say «a pair of» with binoculars? | Binoculars are always very heavy | *Binoculars are plural, with one telescope for each eye | Binoculars can only be used on Sundays | Binoculars are a kind of shoe
